> Once the wizard can survive to Sokoban or further,
> using the advice as given, where "finding sufficient
> food" isn't any longer an issue, hungerless casting
> is really a _dis_advantage, you'd rather be able to
> use casting to get quickly unsatiated from the last
> large prey eaten, so you can eat the next one.

I disagree. Perhaps I've learned my lesson from killing off a
promising priestess by choking on a frost giant corpse, but I now
prefer to deal with large corpses by tinning. Yes, the tinning kit is
extra weight, but if it makes a difference between being borderline
stressed or gaining disintegration resistance or another x points of
giant strength, I'll do it. If no tinning kit, a ring of hunger can be
useful once uncursed. Though generally I'll wear a ring of slow
digestion as soon as I find one, and only take it off when I need to
eat something large and don't have a tinning kit.

Ascending several vegetarians, including one strict vegan, has also
made me somewhat more concerned about finding adequate food supplies
than many posters here. :-)

